    "ls|LS16_S11_U_111": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 111 \nANSWERED ON  2ND FEBRUARY, 2017 \n  \nFOOT OVERBRIDGES ON NATIONAL HIGHWAYS \n \n111.  PROF. PREM SINGH CHANDUMAJRA: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसडक��परिवहन��औि��िाजमार्ग��मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has undertaken work relating to widening and development of \nNational Highways; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the funds allocated therefor; \n(c) whether the National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) proposes to build foot \noverbridges to check fatalities on National Highways and make the journey on them \nsmooth; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof indicating the number of foot overbridges  to be constructed and \nfunds allocated, State-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a) to (b)  Yes Madam. About 1180 nos. of work relating to widening and development of \nNational Highways (NHs) are ongoing. State-wise & scheme -wise a llocation of funds  for \nwidening and development of National Highways are at Annexure-I.       \n(c) to (d)   Yes Madam. 443 numbers of Foot Over Bridges (FOBs) are proposed to be \nconstructed all over the country on NHs by NHAI in a phased manner depending upon the inter -\nse-priorities of works, fulfilling the technical requirements and availability of funds. No separate \nState-wise funds are allocated for FOBs.  \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (b) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 111 ANSWERED ON 2.2.2017 ASKED BY PROF. PREM \nSINGH CHANDUMAJRA  REGARDING FOOT OVERBRIDGES ON NATIONAL \nHIGHWAYS. \n \nState-wise and Scheme -wise Allocation of funds for widening & development of National \nHighways during 2016-17 \n \nSl. No. States/ UTs /Schemes \n/Agency \nAllocation (Crore) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 2,010.31 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 100.00 \n3 Assam 247.44 \n4 Bihar 1,397.43 \n5 Chhattisgarh 1,323.68 \n6 Goa 700.00 \n7 Gujarat 251.87 \n8 Haryana 150.00 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 250.95 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 49.00 \n11 Jharkhand 200.00 \n12 Karnataka 983.38 \n13 Kerala 262.64 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 1,725.00 \n15 Maharashtra 1,851.92 \n16 Manipur 30.25 \n17 Meghalaya 41.27 \n18 Mizoram 30.00 \n19 Nagaland 50.00 \n26 Tripura 40.00 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 2,334.62 \n28 Uttarakhand 342.62 \n29 West Bengal 1,355.71 \n30 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 0.00 \n31 Chandigarh 2.00 \n32 Delhi 2.00 \n33 Puducherry 20.00 \n34 Other projects under NH(O) 2,142.00 \n35  NHAI- Cess  7,476.60 \n36  NHAI- Toll  7,500.00 \n37  NHAI- NH(O)  3,750.00 \n39  SARDP-NE   4,520.00 \n40  LWE   760.00 \n41  EAP  116.38 \n \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_112": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 112\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.02.2017\nGUIDELINES OF PMGSY\n*112. SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI:\nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has issued any fresh directions/guidelines to various States for\nidentification of villages and selection of roads for implementation of the Pradhan Mantri\nGram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) the status of implementation of the scheme in various States including Rajasthan; and\n(c) whether some States have raised objections in regard to the implementation of the said\nscheme and if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nStatement in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 112 for 09.02.2017.\nNo Sir, the Government has not issued any new guidelines for identification of villages and selection\nof roads for implementation of Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY).\nPMGSY was launched in 2000 with the objective to provide a single all -weather road connectivity to\nall eligible unconnected habitations, existing in the Core Network, in rural areas of the country.  The\nprogramme envisages connecting all eligible unconnected habitations with a population of 500\npersons and above  (as per 2001 Census) in plain areas and 250 persons and above (as per 2001\nCensus) in  Special Category States (Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram,\nNagaland, Sikkim,Tripura Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir and Uttarakhand), Tribal\n(Schedule-V) areas, the Deser t Areas  (as identified in Desert Development Programme) and in\nSelected Tribal and Backward Districts (as identified by the Ministry of Home Affairs/Planning\nCommission). The PMGSY permits upgradation (to prescribed standards) of existing rural roads in\ndistricts where all the eligible habitations of the designated population size have been provided all\nweather road connectivity. For most intensive IAP blocks as identified by the Ministry of Home\nAffairs the unconnected habitations with population 100 and above (as per 2001 Census) would be\neligible to be covered under PMGSY.\nSince inception of the PMGSY, (upto December, 2016) project proposals of the value of Rs.\n209,447.71 crore for connecting 1,56,273 habitations, have been sanctioned by the Ministry ,\nagainst which the Ministry has released Rs. 145,184.60 Crore. States have reported completion\nof 4,90,187.65 km of rural roads with an expe nditure of Rs. 1,50,447.96 crore by connecting\n1,21,241 habitations, State –wise details including that of Rajasthan is at Annexure.\n\nAnnexure referred in Lok Sabha Starred Question No 112 (12th Position) due for reply on 9.2.2017\nStatement showing Physical & Financial progress under PMGSY\nRs. In Crore, Length in Km. & Habitation in No.\nSr.No. State Name Value of\nproposals\ncleared (MoRD\nShare)\nValue of\nproposals\ncleared (State\nShare)\nTotal Value cleared Habitations\ncleared\nHabitations\nconnected\nLength of road\nworks\ncompleted\nAmount\nReleased\nExpenditure\n1 Andhra Pradesh 3,795.57 262.44 4,058.01 1,181 1,038 13,574.62 3,023.37 2,953.89\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 5,237.69 2.66 5,240.35 463 368 5,491.33 2,699.53 2,819.29\n3 Assam 9,856.58 547.01 10,403.59 9,997 8,938 16,275.98 8,906.00 9,333.88\n4 Bihar 27,273.45 416.20 27,689.64 29,439 16,667 40,877.79 18,990.73 19,517.10\n5 Chhattisgarh 9,762.50 208.07 9,970.57 10,133 8,873 26,719.98 6,775.51 7,777.88\n6 Goa 15.35 0.00 15.35 2 2 155.33 10.00 0.00\n7 Gujarat 3,365.74 168.00 3,533.75 3,059 3,021 12,343.70 2,953.08 3,418.67\n8 Haryana 2,164.50 300.45 2,464.95 1 1 5,528.42 1,890.70 2,157.61\n9 Himachal Pradesh 3,597.50 22.52 3,620.03 2,232 2,047 11,938.29 2,464.13 2,502.16\n10 Jammu & Kashmir 8,107.42 13.63 8,121.05 2,202 1,469 6,813