    "ls|LS16_S11_U_118": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 118\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2017\nPUBLIC TRANSPORT FACILITIES IN RURAL AREAS\n118. SHRI ABHISHEK SINGH:\nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Union Government is aware that many rural areas in the country still do\nnot have proper 24 hour public transport connectivity even though they are properly\nconnected with rural roads and if so, the details thereof and the steps proposed to be\ntaken by the Union Government thereon; and\n(b) the steps taken or proposed to be taken by the Government to create and develop\nbetter public transport facilities in rural areas to complement the road infrastructure\ndeveloped under Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY)?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV)\n(a) & (b): The Government of India is implementing Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak\nYojana (PMGSY), a centrally sponsored scheme, for providing connectivity to habitations\nhaving minimum prescribed population in rural areas through all weather roads. Provision of\nadequate and reliable transport services on rural roads is the responsibility of t he concerned\nState Governments. However, a proposal is under consideration to involve members of Self\nHelp Groups formed under Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – National Rural Livelihoods\nMission (DAY-NRLM) in providing safe and community monitored public trans port services\nto connect remote villages with services and markets which will give a fillip to overall\neconomic development of the area.\n*****",
