    "ls|LS16_S11_U_173": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *173 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 14TH MARCH, 2017 / PHALGUNA 23, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nCOMMUNICATION WITH CAPF \n \n*173.   SHRI A. ARUNMOZHITHEVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to establish a direct line of \ncommunication between officials of various  hierarchical levels with the top \nechelon in  the Central Armed Police Force (CAPF)  and if so, the details \nthereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government is developing a mobile application which could \nbe used by CAPF personnel and officers to air their grievances and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and  \n \n(c) whether all security aspects are  being taken  into account while  \nintroducing such application and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*173 FOR 14.3.2017. \n \n \n(a) to (c): All the Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) have in place \nappropriate channels of communication  between men and officers in \nrespective organisations. Apart from direct forms of communication/ \ninteraction such as Open Darbar, Sainik Sammelan and personal h earing \netc, which are part of established fora of communication/interaction at \nvarious levels, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) based \ncommunication such as web -based/app-based grievance redressal, mobile \nservices, e-mail etc are also put in use with due security audit as per rules.   \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_175": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION Q. No. *175 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 14.03.2017 \n  \n  Wildlife Protection \n \n \n*175  SHRI P. R. SUNDARAM: \n                                   \n Will the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n  \n(a)   whether the Government has taken scientific and innovative measures to control Wild \nAnimal-Human conflict in the country and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether the Government has provided adequate funds and infrastructure facilities to \ndevelop the wild life and Bird sanctuaries, Zoological parks in the country to protect \nendangered animals and birds; \n(c) if so, the details of funds allocated and released for the purpose during each of  the last \nthree years and the current year, sanctuary/zoological parks and State- wise; and  \n(d)   the steps taken by the Government to develop Marine parks, Zoological parks and bird \nsanctuaries in the country including Tamil Nadu?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF S TATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST \nAND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI ANIL MADHAV DAVE) \n \n \n(a), (b), (c) and (d)  \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS ( a), (b), (c) AND ( d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *175 REGARDING “WILDLIFE \nPROTECTION” RAISED BY SHRI P. R. SUNDARAM  DUE FOR REPLY ON \n14.03.2017. \n \n(a) \n \nThe management of wildlife in the country is taken up in a scientific manner \nby the respective State/Union Territory Govern ments. The Ministry of \nEnvironment, Forest and Climate Change has issued advisories to the \nState/Union Territory Governments for management of human wildlife \nconflict situations. These advisories also indicate the following  important \nactions broadly aiming adoption of scientific principles: \ni. Use of local data in special patterns at Division/Range level with GIS \nbased system.  \nii. Radio telemetry for identification and pattern of  movement of large \nwildlife in case of threat to humans. \niii. Maintaining foraging ground s within forests along boundaries and \naugmenting palatable grasses.  \niv. Identifying and upkeep of wildlife movement corridors, especially \nmigratory patterns. \nv. Payment of ecosystem services principles as an option indentified  \nareas, for encou raging land owners for adopting desirable land use \npractices. In community interest. \n \n(b) and (c) Ministry provides financial assistance to State /Union Territory  \nGovernments  under  various Centrally Sponsored   Scheme viz., Integrated \nDevelopment of Wildlife Habitats (ID WH), ‘Project Tiger ’ and ‘Project \nElephant’ for the scientific management of  wildlife habitats including \ndevelopment of infrastructure  facilities  for wildlife  conservation.   Funds \nare also released for management of Zoological Parks in  the country. Sta te-\nwise details of fund released under these schemes during the last three years \nand the current year is given in the Annexure.   \n(d) Development of Protected Areas including Marine Parks, Zoological Parks \nare the responsibility of the respective state s/operators. However, in case of \nZoological Parks, The Central Zoo Authority provides recognitions as pe r \nprovisions of Wild Life (Protection) Act, 1972. Financial and technical \nassistance is provided by the Ministry/Central Zoo Authority for \nmanagement of Protected Areas and Zoological Parks.  \n \n \n     *** \n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. * 175 \nREGARDING “WILDLIFE PROTECTION” RAISED BY SHRI P. R. SUNDARAM DUE FOR REPLY ON \n14.03.2017. \nDetails of funds released to State/ UT Governments under CSS-‘Integrated Development of Wildlife Habitats’ during \nlast three years and the current yea