    "ls|LS16_S11_U_30": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI,\nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 30\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 03RD FEBRUARY, 2017\nFOREIGN INVESTMENT IN AYURVEDIC TREATMENT CENTRES\n*30. SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL:\nWill the Minister of AYURVEDA, YOGA AND NATUROPATHY,\nUNANI, SIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY (AYUSH) be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has taken adequate steps to popularise Ayurveda\nabroad and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) whether th e Government proposes to allow Foreign Direct Investment\nincluding foreign capital venture to start low cost ayurvedic treatment centres;\n(c) if so, the details thereof along with the places identified for the purpose; and\n(d) whether the Government proposes to issue any directives in this regard and if\nso, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF AYURVEDA,\nYOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI, SIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY\n(SHRI SHRIPAD YESSO NAIK)\n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 30 FOR 3RD FEBRUARY, 2017\na): Yes. In line with its mandate, the Ministry of AYUSH has taken several steps\nto  promote and propagate Ayurveda and other AYUSH systems of medicine\nacross the globe, including signing of Memorandums of Understandings (MOUs)\nfor ‘Country to Country’ cooperation in the field of Traditional Medicines; setting\nup of AYUSH Academic Chairs in foreign Universities/ Educati onal  Institutes;\nestablishing  AYUSH Information Cells in the premises of Indian Missions abroad\nor Indian Cultural Centres for dissemination of authentic information about\nAYUSH systems of medicine. MOUs for collaborative research have also been\nsigned w ith the foreign Universities/ Institutes. Besides above, the Ministry of\nAYUSH organizes/ participates in International exhibitions/ conferences/\nworkshops/seminars/ road shows/ trade fairs etc. to have wider reach for\ninternational propagation of AYUSH an d provides incentives to AYUSH drug\nmanufactures/ entrepreneurs/AYUSH institutions etc. (a) for participating in\nInternational exhibitions/ conferences/ workshops/ seminars road shows/ trade fairs\netc. for generating awareness amongst the participating pub lic about the Indian\nMedicines and; (b) for registration of AYUSH products with regulatory agencies of\ndifferent countries for enhancing export of these products.\n(b) to (d): No such proposal is under consideration of the Government.\n--------",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_31": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *31 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FRIDAY, THE 3rd FEBRUARY, 2017 \n                                                         14TH MAGHA, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nEnrolment under GST \n \n*31.        SHRI DINESH TRIVEDI: \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state:  \n \na) the number of assesses who have enrolled for the new Goods and Services Tax \n(GST) regime on the e-Government portal of the Central Excise and Service Tax; \nb) the details of different medium such as website, phone applications, physical  \ncentres available for these registrants; and \nc) the initiatives being taken by the Government to increase the registrants for  the \nGST regime? \n \nANSWER \nFINANCE MINISTER \n(SHRI ARUN JAITLEY) \n \n \na) By 3:00 PM on 31 st January 2017, 43.4 Lakh taxpayers registered under State \nVAT, Central Excise and Service Tax have enrolled on GST portal www.gst.gov.in \nfor the new GST regime. \n \nb) Existing taxpayers can enroll themselves for GST through the following modes: \n \ni. On GST portal at www.gst.gov.in through internet;  \nii. Through Mobile application which can be downloaded free from www.gst.gov.in. \n \nc) The initiatives taken by Central and State tax departments are: \n \ni. Awareness through print and electronic media.  \nii. Workshops organized by the tax  departments for their taxpayers/ trade and \nindustry associations.  \niii. Email and SMS to existing taxpayers. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_32": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI,\nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 32\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 03RD FEBRUARY, 2017\nAYUSH HOSPITALS\n*32. SHRI C.R. PATIL:\nSHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN:\nWill the Minister of AYURVEDA, YOGA AND NATUROPATHY,\nUNANI, SIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY (AYUSH) be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of AYUSH hospitals/ dispensaries including research centres\nfunctioning at present in the country, stream-wise and State/UT-wise;\n(b) whether the Government has received a number of proposals from various\nStates for upgradation/setting up of new AYUSH hospitals/dispensaries and if so,\nthe details thereof State/U T-wise along with the response of the Government\nthereto;\n(c) whether the Government proposes to open new hospitals, dispensaries and\nresearch centres in various States of the country and if so, the details thereof, State/\nUT-wise, location-wise and stream-wise; and\n(d) the funds earmarked for the purpose along with the time by which the said\ninstitutions are likely to be started?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF AYURVEDA,\nYOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI, SIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY\n(SHRI SHRIPAD YESSO NAIK)\n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 32 FOR 3RD FEBRUARY, 2017\n(a) The details of AYUSH hospitals/ dispensaries including research centres\nfunctioning at present in the country, stream-wise and State/UT-wise is enclosed as\nAnnexure –I.\n(b) Yes. The number of proposals received by the Government under Centrally\nSponsored Scheme of National AYUSH Mission from various States for\nupgradation/setting up of new AYUSH hospitals /dispensaries, State/UT-wise\nduring current year is furnished at Annexure-II.\n(c) Health is a State subject. However, under Centrally Sponsored Scheme of\nNational AYUSH Mission (NAM), there is a provision of setting up o f 50 bedded\nintegrated AYUSH Hospital. During the current year, Government of India has\nprovided financial assistance for the component of setting up of 30 integrated\nAYUSH hospitals in 18 States/UTs as per the detail furnished at Annexure-III.\nFurther, Government has approved setting up of Post Graduate Institute of Y oga\nand Naturopathy Education and Research at Nagmangla (Karnataka) and Jhajjar\n(Haryana).\n(d) Rs. 400.00 Crore has been earmarked under National AYUSH Mission (NAM)\nfor different activities including upgradation/setting up of new AYUSH\nhospitals/dispensaries during current year . Implementation of approved projects\ncomes under purview of State/UT Governments. Further, the total cost approved\nfor setting up of the institutes at Nagmangla (Karnataka) and Jhajjar (Haryana) are\nRs. 59.67 Crores and Rs. 52.04 crores respectively.\n\nAnnexure-I\nState wise/System wise Number of AYUSH Hospitals as on 1-4-2016\nS.\nNo.\nState / UT\nAyurveda Unani Siddha Yoga Naturopathy Homoeopathy Sowa-\nRigpa Total\nA. States/Union Territories\n1 Andhra Pradesh 3 2 0 0 0 3 0 8\n2\nArunachal\nPradesh 10 0 0 0 0 2 0 12\n3 Assam 1 0 0 0 0 3 0 4\n4 Bihar 5 1 0 0 0 2 0 8\n5 Chhattisgarh 9 1 0 1 0 3 0 14\n6 Delhi 2 1 0 0 0 2 0 5\n7 Goa 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n8 Gujarat 42 0 0 0 6 16 0 64\n9 Haryana 9 1 0 0 0 1 0 11\n10\nHimachal\nPradesh 31 0 0 0 1 0 0 32\n11\nJammu &\nKashmir 1 1 0 0 0 0 0 2\n12 Jharkhand 1 0 0 0 0 4 0 5\n13 Karnataka 170 18 0 3 6 16 0 213\n14 Kerala 124 0 1 0 1 31 0 157\n15 Madhya Pradesh 21 0 0 0 0 2 0 23\n16 Maharashtra 63 6 0 0 0 46 0 115\n17 Manipur 0 2 0 0 13 7 0 22\n18 Meghalaya 3 0 0 0 0 7 0 10\n19 Mizoram 0 0 0 0 0 8 0 8\n20 Nagaland 0 0 0 0 0 2 0 2\n21 Odisha 8 0 0 0 0 6 0 14\n22 Punjab 5 0 0 0 0 4 0 9\n23 Rajasthan 118 11 0 1 2 6 0 138\n24 Sikkim 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1\n25 Tamil Nadu 2 1 271 1 0 1 0 276\n26 Tripura 2 0 0 0 0 2 0 4\n27 Uttar Pradesh 1771 204 0 0 0 8 0 1983\n28 Uttarakhand 402 2 0 0 0 1 0 405\n29 West Bengal 6 1 0 0 0 12 1 20\n30 A&N Islan