    "ls|LS16_S11_U_7": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 \nANSWERED ON 2ND FEBRUARY, 2017 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF NATIONAL HIGHWAYS \n \n*7.  SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to develop the National Highways so as to meet international \nstandards and if so, the action taken thereon; \n(b) whether  the Government proposes to seek private participation in the development of the \nNational Highways and if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the present status of construction of Kollam Bypass project and the expected date of completion \nthereof; \n(d) the details of the action taken by the Government for the development  of Kollam -\nThirumangalam National Highway; and \n(e) the details of proposed development and amount sanctioned for the development of National \nHighways, especially in Kollam?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n (a) to (e)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED T O IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( e) OF LOK SABHA STARR ED \nQUESTION NO. 7 ANSWERED ON 02.02.2017 ASKED BY SHRI N. K. PREMACHANDRAN \nREGARDING DEVELOPMENT OF NATIONAL HIGHWAYS \n \n(a)  The development and maintenance of National Highways (NHs) is a continuous process. \nThe works on NHs are accordingly taken up from time to time as per inter-se priority, traffic density \nand availability of funds to keep the NHs in traffic worthy conditions. \n  \n            The Ministry has taken up development of NHs under various phases of National Highways \nDevelopment Project (NHDP), Special Accelerated Road Development Prog ramme for the North \nEast Region (SARDP-NE) including Arunachal Pradesh Package of Roads, Special Programme for \nDevelopment of Roads in the Left Wing Extremism (LWE) affected areas, National Highways \nInterconnectivity Improvement Project (NHIIP), etc. \n   \n There are two National Expressways (NE) at present. NE -1 (Ahmedabad - Vadodara \nExpressway), having 93.4 km length, was developed as 4 lane Expressway in 2004 and is under \noperation; works for construction of NE -2 ( Eastern Peripheral Expressway in the States  of Uttar \nPradesh and Haryana, connecting NH-1 and NH-2), of about 135  km length, have been awarded in \nAugust, 2015 and is targeted for completion in March, 2018.  The details of ongoing / planned \nprojects for development of Expressways, sanctioned cost of  ongoing projects, along with their \ncurrent status is annexed. \n   \n(b) Public Private Partnerships (PPP) continue to be the preferred model for developing \nhighways today, leveraging the advantages of private sector involvement by way of harnessing \noverall m anagerial prowess, operational efficiency, sector specific expertise, investment potential \nand opportunity for appropriate allocation of risks between the partners. However, Highway Sector \nhad witnessed a steep decline in PPP participation in 2012 -13 and 2 013-14 with many viable \nprojects unable to attract even a single bid. \n \nThe compara tively lower response to PPP mode in the recent past is due to economic \nreasons, non-availability of equity with the concessionaires and other construction, land acquisition \nand regulatory clearances related issues. Under such a situation, the Government takes up road \nprojects under Engineering, Procurement, Construction (EPC) mode and Hybrid Annuity Model  \n(HAM), when the project is not found viable on PPP under Build -Operate-Transfer (BOT) (Toll) \nmode. HAM is sometimes preferred as it enables achievement of greater length of highway \nconstruction as compared to EPC mode due to its lower initial capital investment requirements. \n  \nWhile, BOT (Toll) mode continues to be the default mode, other modes are chosen when \nany project is not found viable on BOT (Toll). \n \n(c)  The scheduled date of completion of ongoing project of construction of Kollam Bypass is \n26.11.2017. \n \n(d) and (e)  The preparation of Detailed Project Report (DPR ) has been taken up for \ndevelopment of Kollam -Thirumangalam section of NH 208 (new NH 744)  in state of Kerala . \nDevelopment of NH 47(new NH 66)  passing through Kollam Constituency to 4-lane NH standards \nis included under NHDP Phase -III and its DPR preparation has been taken up.  The work of \npreparation of DPR for development to two lane with paved shoulder of Kollam to Anjilimoodu \nsection of NH 220  in the Kollam Constituency  has also been taken up . Resurfacing work s from \nKadambattukonam to Krishnapur am of NH 47, from Kollam to Anjilimoodu of NH 220 (new NH \n183) and from Ezhukone to Punalur of NH 208 (new NH 744) passing through this constituency \nhave been completed recently for sanctioned costs of about Rs. 46.35 crore, Rs. 34.09 crore and Rs. \n8.66 crore respectively.    \n \n    \n\n \n \nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 7 \nANSWERED ON 02.02.2017 ASKED BY SHRI N.K PREMACHANDRAN REGARDING \nDEVELOPMENT OF NATIONAL HIGHWAYS \n(I) Details of ongoing projects for development of Expressways: - \n \nName of \nExpressway \nExp. Way \n/NH No. \n \nName of \nStretch \nLength \n(km) \nSanctioned \ncost \n(Rs in crore) \nDate of \naward \nScheduled \ndate of \ncompletion \nEastern \nPeripheral \nExpressway \n(Package-I to VI) \nNE-II EPE 135  5,763.10 August, \n2015 \nMarch, \n2018 \nDelhi-Meerut \nExpressway \n(Package-I) \nNH-24 Delhi- Delhi/UP \nBorder \n \n8.716 701.12 January, \n2016 \nMay, 2019 \nDelhi-Meerut \nExpressway \n(Package-III) \nNH-24 Delhi/UP \nBorder to \nDasana \n22.27  1,081.57 January, \n2016 \nJune, 2019 \n \nII) Details of projects planned for development of Expressways: -   \n \nName of Expressway Expressway/\nNH No. \nLength \n(km) \nCurrent Status  \nDelhi-Meerut \nExpressway Pkg-II \nNH-24  \n19.284 \n Financial Bids opened on 08.11.2016 \n One bidder has filed CWP in Hon’ble \nHigh Court of Delhi \n The Hon'ble High Court has reserved \nits judgement in its hearing on 06.12.2016 and \nthe judgment is awaited. \n \nDelhi-Meerut \nExpressway Pkg-IV \nNew \nAlignment \n46.056 Bids invited on EPC Mode and the bid due \ndate is 16.02.2017 \n \nVadodara-Mumbai \nExpressway \nNew \nAlignment \n473.062  DPR preparation taken up \nBangalore-Chennai \nExpressway \nNew \nAlignment \n264.278 DPR preparation taken up \nDelhi-Jaipur \nExpressway \nNew \nAlignment \n226.67  \n \nDPR preparation taken up \nDelhi-Ludhiana-\nAmritsar-Katra with \nconnectivity to \nChandigarh Expressway \nNew \nAlignment \n-- Bid invited for taking up Feasibility Study \nKolkata-\nDhanbadExpressway \nNew \nAlignment \n-- DPR preparation taken up. \nNagpur-Hyderabad-\nBangalore Expressway \nNew \nAlignment \n-- Bid invited for taking up Feasibility Study \nHyderabad-Vijayawada-\nAmravathi Expressway \nNew \nAlignment \n-- In first call no bidder qualified. Then bid with \nmodified documents being reinvited. \nLucknow-Kanpur \nExpressway \nNew \nAlignment \n-- Bid invited for taking up Feasibility Study \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_70": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                MINISTRY OF SHIPPING \n \n            LOK SABHA  \n                UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.70 \n             ANSWERED ON 2nd FEBRUARY, 2017 \nDEVELOPMENT OF VADINAR PORT  \n70.  SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN:  \nWill the Minister of SHIPPING  be pleased to state: \nपोतप�रवहनमंत् \n(a)  the present status of the proposal for development of Vadinar Port as a joint \nventure between Kandla Port Trust and Gujarat Maritime Board; and \n(b)  the time by which the said proposal is likely to be approved? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SHIPPING \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a) Kandla Port Trust has not received any detailed proposal for Development of \nVadinar Port as joint venture between Kandla Port Trust and Gujarat Maritime \nBoard,  \n \n \n(b) In view of (a) does not arise. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S11_U_71": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n71\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n7\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY, 2017\n \n \n \nDISTRESS SALE OF AGRICULTURAL PRODUCE\n \n \n*71. \n    \nSHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN: \n \n            \nSHRI HARISH MEENA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \n½ãâ¨ããè\n  \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether widespread distress sale of agricultural produce including vegetables have \nbeen reported in the rural areas due to demonetisation and also for want of remunerative \nprices and if so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the agriculture labourers have reportedly been idle/retrenched due to \ndemonetisation and if so the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has analysed the financial losses suffered by farmers due \nto demonetisation and if so, the details the\nreof; and \n \n \n(d) \n \nthe steps taken by the Government to provide compensation and adequate \nremunerative prices to the farmers?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n  \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI RADHA MOHAN SINGH\n)\n \n \n \n(a) to (d\n):\n \nA \nstatement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. \n \n71\n  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n7\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY, 2017\n.\n \n \n(a):  \n   \nNo widespread distress sale of agricultural produce including that of \nvegetables has been \nreported in the rural areas due to demonetisation. Price is determined by demand and supply \nand Government has in place a mechanism  to protect the farmers from distress sale by \nprocuring agricultural produce through Central/State agenc\nies under Price Support Scheme \n(PSS) and Market Intervention Scheme (MIS), when price of these commodities fall below \nMinimum Support Price and Cost of Production respectively.  The payments to the farmers are \nmade strictly through Real Time Gross Settleme\nnt (RTGS)/National Electronic Fund Transfer \n(NEFT) and account payee cheque by the procuring agencies.\n \n \n(b): \n \n  \nNo such retrenchment of the agriculture labourers has been reported. The total area \nsown under five major crop\n-\ncategories in Rabi was higher tha\nn the same period last year\n.\n \n \n(c): \n \n   \nQuestion does not arise.\n \n \n(d): \n       \nThere was no situation that warranted payment of compensation to the farmers.\n \n \n \n \nAs regards ensuring remunerative prices to the farmers, Government has been working \non improving t\nhe marketing environment in the Agriculture Produce Market Committee \n(APMCs) markets.  With this objective, Government has launched eNAM on 14.04.2016, under \nwhich online trading of agriculture produce is being undertaken. By now 250 number of APMCs \nhave b\neen integrated on the electronic National Agriculture Market (eNAM) platform. \nGovernment is also working on a new APMC Model Act with a view to creating an efficient \nagriculture marketing system in the country and enable the farmers to realise remunerative\n \nprices. \n \n \nApart from the above, Government also notifies Minimum Support Price (MSP) for 2\n3\n \ncommodities covering both Kharif and Rabi seasons.  The Government has put in place a \nsystem of procurement, whenever price fall below MSP.  Procurement operations are \nundertaken by FCI in case of wheat and paddy. Under Price Support Scheme (PSS), \nprocure\nment of pulses and oilseeds is undertaken whenever State Governments report that \nprices have fallen below MSP. National Agricultural Cooperative Marketing Federation of India \n(NAFED) undertakes such procurement.  In case of perishable commodities where MSP\n \nis not \nnotified, procurement is undertaken under Market Intervention Scheme (MIS). In addition, \nprocurement undertaken by Department of Consumer Affairs under Price Stabilisation Fund \n(PSF) is also found to be useful in assisting the farmers remunerative \nprice.\n \n******\n ",
