    "ls|LS16_S11_U_88": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nLOK  SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 88 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 08, 2017 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF SLUMS \n \nNo. 88.   SHRI B.V. NAIK: \nDR. VIRENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUS ING AND URBAN POVERTY \nALLEVIATION be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of slums and the population of slum dwellers in the \ncountry, State-wise; \n(b) the number of slums demolished during the last three years and \nthe amount of compensation disbursed, State-wise and year-wise; \n(c) the fund disbursed for constru ction of low cost housing during \nthe last three years and the number  of houses constructed, State-\nwise and year-wise; \n(d) whether the percentage of slum population has changed over the \nlast three times of data collection at All India and State levels and if \nso, the details thereof; and \n(e) the programmes and schemes r un by the Ministry for slum \ndevelopment, rehabilitation and impr ovement of socio-economic \nconditions of slum dwellers and funds allocated for the same during \nthe last three years, State-wise? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n[SHRI M.VENKAIAH NAIDU] \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is la id on the Table of the Sabha. \n******  \nContd…. \n\n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 88* FOR 08.02.2017 REGARDING “DEVELOPMENT OF \nSLUMS” \n******* \n \n(a): As per NSSO Report on “Urban Slum in India-2012”, the total \nestimated no. of slums in the country is 33,510.  As per Census-2011 \ndata, the slum population is 6,54,94,604.  \n(b): Housing, land & colonis ation being Stat e Subject, the \ndemolition of slums and compensat ion thereof comes under the \npurview of State Governments.   \n(c): State/UT-wise and year-wis e details of fund released and \nhouses constructed during the last three years under the Schemes \nof Jawaharlal Nehru National Urban Renewal Mission (JNNURM), \nRajiv Awas Yojana (RAY) and Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana \n(Urban)[PMAY(U)] is at Annexure-1.  \n(d):   As per the Census 2001 data, slum population was 18.30% of \ntotal urban population in the country .  As per Census 2011, this is \n17.4%.  State-wise Urban Popul ation, Slum Population and \npercentage of Slum Population in  urban population during Census \n2001 and 2011 are at Annexure-2.   \n(e): The Central Government through its schemes provides \nassistance to States/UTs in addr essing the housing requirement of \nthe slum dwellers and urban poor.  To achieve this goal, \nGovernment of India had im plemented the JNNURM with two \ncomponents viz. Basic Services to the Urban Poor (BSUP) and \nIntegrated Housing and Slum Development Programme (IHSDP). \n \nContd.. \n\n-3- \nMission duration was 7 years from 2005-06 which has been \nextended upto March, 2017 for co mpletion of projects sanctioned \nupto March, 2012.   \nGovernment also implemented Rajiv Awas Yojana (RAY) for \nproviding houses along with basic ci vic and social infrastructure for \nslum dwellers and urban poor.  Rajiv Awas Yojana has been \ndiscontinued and liabilities agains t 183 ongoing RAY projects have \nbeen subsumed in PMAY-HFA (U). \nIn pursuance of the Government’s vision of facilitating housing to all \nby 2022, the Government is im plementing PMAY(U).  The Mission \naims to provide assistance to St ates/UTs in addressing the housing \nrequirement of the slum dwellers and urban poor. \nState-wise details of the fund sa nctioned during last three years \nunder JNNURM, RAY & PMAY(U) Mission is at Annexure-3. \n****** \n \n \n \n \n\n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16\n1 A&N Island (UT) -              -               -               -             -             -             \n2 Andhra Pradesh 17.34          64.79           335.90         2,439         2,876         3,758         \n3 Arunanchal Pradesh 25.69          32.11           -               -       